            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "It appears the D-Bus sensors code will throw an exception and probably just crash if one of these properties aren't on the interface, so they should probably all be required?  \n\nThough I guess it isn't any worse than what was there previously, and saves you from having to look at the implementing code for every one of these commits."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/legacy.json",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "> It appears the D-Bus sensors code will throw an exception and probably just crash if one of these properties aren't on the interface, so they should probably all be required? \n\nSince you made that effort to look at the code, i adjusted them all (besides Thresholds) to be required \ud83d\ude0a\n\n> Though I guess it isn't any worse than what was there previously, and saves you from having to look at the implementing code for every one of these commits.\n\nYes, that was my intention. I want to first extract a basic schema from ```Aggregate``` so that the ```Aggregate``` schema will get smaller.\n\nThen we can have more specific schemas for different configurations.\n\nAs time goes on, these can be further refined. If there is any comment from people who have some knowledge of the dbus-sensors code, i can adjust ```required``` as needed."
                }
            ],
